le: a power iteration (eigenvector and Katz centrality, PageRank, HITS), a Lanczos"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or conjugate-gradient run, or a QL eigenvalue iteration. Named after Eigen’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ComputationInfo::NoConvergence"},{"type":"text","text":"; NetworkX raises "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PowerIterationFailedConvergence"},{"type":"text","text":" and SciPy"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ArpackNoConvergence"},{"type":"text","text":" in the same place."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"NoConvergence","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/noconvergence","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NoConvergence"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NoConvergence"}]},"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory/GraphProtocols":{"abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols","title":"GraphProtocols","url":"\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols"},"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory":{"abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory","title":"SpectralGraphTheory","url":"\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory"},"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory/FiedlerVector":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The Fiedler vector of a connected graph: a unit eigenvector of λ₂, the algebraic","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"connectivity, of the Laplacian (or of the normalized Laplacian), with one entry per vertex.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/FiedlerVec